---
import type { GetStaticPaths } from 'astro';
import LegalLayout from '../../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { LOCALES } from '../../../i18n/utils';
import { resolveLocale } from '../../../lib/page';

export const getStaticPaths: GetStaticPaths = () => LOCALES.map((lang) => ({ params: { lang } }));

const locale = resolveLocale(Astro.params.lang);
const dateModified = '2026-09-28';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookies"
  description="No cookies, no consent banner, no advertising or analytics scripts. What is stored, where, and what must change before any analytics tool is ever added."
  locale={locale}
  path="/legal/cookies"
  dateModified={dateModified}
  icon="database"
>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">No cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no cookies. None. Not for preferences, not for sessions, not for measurement, not
    for advertising. There is no first-party storage and no third-party storage.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no consent banner, because a banner would be a lie: there is nothing to consent to. If
    you have seen one here, you were looking at a different site.
  </p>

  <h2 class="pt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">The one thing we do store</h2>
  <p>
    Your light or dark theme choice, in your browser's local storage, under the key
    <code class="tabular">cg-theme</code>. It stays on your device, it is never transmitted, and it is
    removed when you clear site data for the site. It is not a cookie, it is not readable by us, and
    it identifies nobody.
  </p>

  <h2 class="pt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Analytics, and the line we will not cross without changing this page</h2>
  <p>
    There is one measurement activity, and it happens on our servers rather than yours. Request logs
    are truncated and anonymised at the edge before they are stored, and raw logs are deleted after
    30 days. Nothing is loaded into your browser to measure you, so there is nothing to block and
    nothing to consent to.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a client-side analytics tool is ever added — a script in your browser that builds a profile
    and reports it back — then this page must be rewritten first, and a consent mechanism must exist
    before the tool is loaded, not after. German and Austrian visitors are the reason this is stated
    as a hard rule rather than a preference: in those jurisdictions consent must be obtained before
    the first storage, and there is no reading of our current position that would let us skip it.
    We would rather not add such a tool than spend the project's credibility on a consent dialog.
  </p>

  <h2 class="pt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Crawlers, including AI crawlers</h2>
  <p>
    Search engine crawlers and AI crawlers are both welcome. Nothing on this site is blocked for
    being a bot, and no crawler is served a different page from a person. If you quote this site, the
    fair thing is to quote the date on the page and to say the times are scheduled rather than
    observed. That is the whole of our position on citation, and it is set out in full on the
    <a class="underline" href="/data/quality">known limits</a> page.
  </p>
  <p>
    Crawling is not the same as syndication. We do not register or feed our timetable data to Google
    Maps, Apple Maps, Moovit, Transit App or any other aggregator, so a crawler reading our pages will
    find a schedule with a date on it rather than a source that is treated as a departure board. The
    reason is accuracy, and it is explained on the
    <a class="underline" href="/data/open-data">open data</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2 class="pt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Third-party embeds</h2>
  <p>
    There are none. No video embeds, no advertising tags, no chat widgets, no embedded maps that
    phone home, no social media pixels. The map tiles in the island planners are a static asset served
    from our own host, not a live third-party tile service, which is also how they keep working with
    no signal.
  </p>

  <p class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)] pt-4 text-sm">
    <span class="tabular">Date last updated: {dateModified}</span>. If this page ever stops being
    true, that is a bug with a higher priority than most features, and the
    <a class="underline" href="/legal/privacy">privacy notice</a> is the page that has to be updated
    with it.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
